e first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(1)-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=4\\,⟹\\,x=4+1+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{11}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{11}{2}$,  $y=1$, and $z=\\frac{1}{2}.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨\\frac{11}{2},1,\\frac{1}{2}⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237861 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0947bcb2-124b-5a9b-8c2d-caaf1dd4d78e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12,-3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235859} {:answer/id #uuid "4b19167d-8908-5eb5-b1b2-35217d6c79d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9,-3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236299} {:answer/id #uuid "6b66fc33-4c80-5b0f-8c9f-716a423a5b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236494} {:answer/id #uuid "ae0a4fc5-1033-5109-8969-8d7ba972a0fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9,2,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236922} {:answer/id #uuid "d095b16d-d82d-5f43-b45a-419f5d3af373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b66fc33-4c80-5b0f-8c9f-716a423a5b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨11,3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236494} :answer-field/id #uuid "be1426b6-aff3-5cb0-a4a0-23caf436597b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237682}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bcc22116-bc14-5a39-b8c2-56ca9a77cd3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-10198" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=9 \\\\ {x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that  ${x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{3}.$ 